  "narration": "Why did GTA 6 take 13 years to come out?\nIf you were 15 when GTA 5 launched, you’re 28 today.\nIt started In 1995, in Dundee, Scotland,\na young team accidentally made police cars go crazy.\nInstead of chasing you, they loved it, so they kept it.\nand In 1997, the game became Grand Theft Auto.\nIn 1998, Sam and Dan Houser co-founded Rockstar Games.\nAnd in 2001,\nGTA 3 changed gaming with its first fully\n3D open city Vice City followed In 2004, San Andreas went even bigger,\ngiving you 3 cities, and a massive world 3 huge games in 3 years.\nthen things slowed down GTA 4 took 4 years.\nGTA 5 took 5.\nIt introduced 3 playable characters, and made a billion dollars in just 3 days.\nAnd then it kept selling.\nOver 230 million copies later GTA 5 had survived 3 console generations,\nwhile GTA Online kept growing Rockstar then made Red Dead Redemption 2 first.\nWhen GTA 6 finally entered development in September 2022,\neverything went wrong a teenage hacker.\n",
