  "metadata": {
    "title": "Why did GTA 6 take 13 years? From a bug in Scotland in 1995 to November 19, 2026.",
    "description": "Free guide to this video (steps and every source): https://studio.golidee.com/guides/golide-external-2026-11-20-0932.pdf\n\nWhy did GTA 6 take 13 years to come out? This short traces Rockstar Games’ journey from the original Grand Theft Auto in Dundee to GTA 3, Vice City, San Andreas, GTA 4, GTA 5, and Red Dead Redemption 2.\n\nIt explains how GTA 5 and GTA Online kept growing, why Rockstar’s development cycles became longer, and what happened when GTA 6 finally entered serious development—ending with the teenage hacker who changed everything.\n\n#GTA6 #GrandTheftAuto6 #RockstarGames #GTAV #GamingHistory #GameDevelopment #GOLIDE",
